BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Migrantes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T200000
UID:migrantes-2026-12-03t20-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/11
 /MIGRANTES-Colour-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.png?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Migrantes is a musical and narrative experience that explores 
 migration as an inner journey — a movement of the soul as much as of the
  body.\n\nAndrea Manzoni (piano) and Mauro Sigura (oud) create a space whe
 re different musical traditions meet and interact\, becoming part of a bro
 ader reflection on cultural diversity\, migration\, and contemporary forms
  of artistic expression. The performance draws on the rich and diverse bac
 kgrounds of the two musicians\, combining elements of European jazz\, cont
 emporary experimentation\, and the evocative sounds of Arab-Ottoman music 
 creating an original and compelling soundscape.\n\nThrough pulsating rhyth
 ms\, improvisation\, and the constant exchange between piano and oud\, the
  audience is taken through a journey that transcends geographical and cult
 ural boundaries. Migrantes invites audiences to not only listen\, but to e
 nter an immersive experience in which musical traditions encounter one ano
 ther.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/migrantes/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Drumming Workshops
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261206T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261206T130000
UID:drumming-workshops-2026-12-06t13-00-00-05-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/11
 /Fall-Fair-Alnoor-Meralli-098-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?res
 ize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Bring your family and find your inner rhythm by joining us on 
 stage in the Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium for a special drumming wor
 kshop.\n\nJoin artist Amadou Kienou for a hands-on drumming workshop intro
 ducing participants to West African culture and traditions. Learn differen
 t drumming techniques and rhythms on the djembé while connecting with oth
 ers.\n\nThe djembé is more than a musical instrument\, it is a form of co
 mmunication used to send messages from village to village\, city to city\,
  and country to country. Learn about its role in West African culture and 
 how it brings people together through music.
LOCATION:Nanji Family Foundation Auditorium\, Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford
  Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/drumming-workshops/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
